## Context

The MVP must remain usable while some measures migrate. Complete provenance must not push the already large ZAF JSON past the repository cap.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

Export two display IDs sharing a payload/pointer/role across routes plus a repeated same-page instance. Reverse traversal returns all, duplicate display IDs fail, and a partly migrated or duplicate-owned financial combination cannot publish.

## Actions

First deliver traced reported positions from 0764 without waiting for the financial engine. Enabling reconstructed financial combinations additionally requires accepted 0768 outputs. Implement versioned output/renderer compatibility, shared provenance sidecars or bounded chunks, editorial claim evidence, principal/news source roles and accessible glossary. Select publication mode per typed subject/measure/perimeter independently of writer transfer. Preserve routes and complete downloads; consume only accepted candidate inputs. Apply existing 0727 timing-bound/count follow-ups. Implement complete-bundle publication and restoration without reversing evidence ownership.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All published claims resolve through exact evidence/derivation and display IDs
- [ ] Mixed migration has one owner per contribution and no partial reconciled totals
- [ ] Four-country browser routes, filters, timelines and downloads remain viable
- [ ] Payload sizes meet cap with no missing offline dependencies
- [ ] Homepage principal link, country two-role links and total-evidence prose semantics hold
- [ ] Failed candidate leaves accepted bundle intact; rollback preserves newer evidence

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

